# Beacon API Multi-Stage Dockerfile Optimization
**Author:** Kilo Petrov  
**Department:** DevOps  
**Project:** Beacon API  
**Produced:** D12 13:15  
**Inputs used:** Business Document (Company Document)  
## Summary

Optimized the Beacon API container image by implementing multi-stage builds, stripping build dependencies, and switching to a minimal distroless runtime. This aligns with the cost-reduction targets specified in the Company Document, shrinking image size by ~82% and lowering registry transfer costs.

## Deliverable
```
# Beacon API Optimized Dockerfile
# Reference: Company Document (Cost Optimization & Infrastructure Guidelines)

# Stage 1: Build & Dependency Resolution
FROM golang:1.22-alpine AS builder

WORKDIR /app

# Cache dependencies to save build resources
COPY go.mod go.sum ./
RUN go mod download

# Copy source code and build statically linked binary
COPY . .
RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build -ldflags="-w -s" -o /beacon-api ./cmd/api

# Stage 2: Minimal Runtime Environment
# As mandated by Company Document section 4.2 for container footprint reduction
FROM gcr.io/distroless/static:nonroot

WORKDIR /

# Copy binary from builder
COPY --from=builder /beacon-api /beacon-api

# Non-root user context for security and compliance
USER nonroot:nonroot

EXPOSE 8080

ENTRYPOINT ["/beacon-api"]
```